Grayswandir.  Long story short, I finished the quest and castle, and 
minimized saccing so I wouldn't have too many artifacts in the game.  Still 
I blew 4 wishes trying to get the Eye, but finally I got it.

I tried on a [HoOA and became lawful, but saccing at a lawful altar didn't 
seem to get me anything.  I thought maybe the gods didn't like my [HoOA, so 
I took it off and tried a unicorn sacrifice conversion instead.  Worked 
fine, I became lawful and after some time I eventually got Grayswandir.  

Only one problem:  The Eye is on the floor and I can't pick it up.  I 
accidentally dropped the Eye, despite a concscious effort to keep it on my 
person.  But I thought I would be changing back eventually so I didn't 
think too much of it.

I tried changing back to neutral with an appropriate white unicorn 
sacrifice, but Camaxtli would have none of it.  I did get to bask in a 
black glow free of charge, though.

"What do you mean you can only change 'base alignment' once?!"

Is there any possible way for me to pick up the eye now?  Like by having a 
pet or other monster pick it up and polyself-ing into a nymph?  Or any 
